iption":"Trying to decide between a couple of closely ranked players this week? Eric Karabell's ranks are here to help.","published":"2026-11-27T14:03:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50573832/fantasy-football-superflex-rankings-2026-qb-rb-wr-te","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Karabell","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy football rankings Week 12: PPR and superflex","description":"Weekly composite ranks for each position in PPR and IDP formats, as well as Eric Karabell's superflex ranks.","published":"2026-11-27T13:58:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/page/FFWeeklyPlayerRank26main-49797082/fantasy-football-rankings-2026-qb-rb-wr-te-dst","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Fantasy","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Trevor Nowaske","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevor_Nowaske","description":"American football player (born 1998)","touched":"2026-11-26T23:15:21Z","intro":"Trevor Nowaske (born November 7, 1998) is an American professional football linebacker for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Saginaw Valley State Cardinals. He signed with the Detroit Lions as an undrafted free agent in 2023.","sections":[{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"DETROIT LIONS\nOn May 12, 2023, the Detroit Lions signed Nowaske to a three-year, $2.695 million contract as an undrafted free agent. He was waived by Detroit on August 29, and was re-signed to the team's practice squad. On November 2, Nowaske was signed to the active roster. He was waived by the Lions on December 28.\n\nARIZONA CARDINALS\nOn December 29, 2023, Nowaske was claimed off waivers by the Arizona Cardinals. He was waived by the Cardinals on August 27, 2024.\n\nDETROIT LIONS (SECOND STINT)\nOn August 28, 2024, the Detroit Lions claimed Nowaske off waivers. On October 27 against the Tennessee Titans, Nowaske recorded his first interception off of Mason Rudolph.\nOn March 14, 2025, Nowaske re-signed with the Lions.\nOn March 16, 2026, Nowaske re-signed with the Lions."}],"wikidataId":"Q121461325","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-03-13","text":"Signed DB Izien Christian and LB Trevor Nowaske to contracts."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/5144894","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/N/NowaTr00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/trevor-nowaske/169859","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/trevor-nowaske/11481","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevor_Nowaske"},"insights":["Ranks 1st of 79 qualified linebackers in completion % allowed.","Ranks 2nd of 79 qualified linebackers in passer rating allowed.","On the field for 33% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.4M is the 29th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season."]}